 rings around it?','Earth','Mars','Saturn','Mercury','c','Saturn has visible rings.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(837,91,'The Earth’s natural satellite is:','Sun','Star','Moon','Mars','c','Moon is Earth&#039;s natural satellite.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(838,91,'The Moon does not have:','Mountains','Craters','Air and water','Rocky surface','c','Moon lacks air and water.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(839,91,'The Moon shines because it:','Produces light','Reflects sunlight','Has fire','Is a star','b','Moon reflects Sun&#039;s light.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(840,91,'A full moon appears about once every:','7 days','14 days','29 days','365 days','c','Full moon occurs roughly every 29 days.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(841,91,'The shapes of the Moon seen from Earth are called:','Circles','Shadows','Phases','Orbits','c','They are called phases.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(842,91,'Stars are huge balls of:','Ice','Stone','Burning gas','Water','c','Stars are made of burning gases.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(843,91,'The closest star to Earth is:','Polaris','Sirius','Sun','Moon','c','The Sun is closest.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(844,91,'A group of stars forming patterns is called:','Galaxy','Orbit','Constellation','Asteroid','c','Patterns of stars are constellations.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(845,91,'The Milky Way is a:','Planet','Constellation','Galaxy','Star','c','Milky Way is a galaxy.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(846,91,'Our solar system is part of the:','Orion','Ursa Major','Milky Way','Andromeda','c','Solar system lies in Milky Way.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(847,91,'The first Indian to go to space was:','Kalpana Chawla','Rakesh Sharma','Sunita Williams','Sirisha Bandla','b','Rakesh Sharma went in 1984.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(848,91,'The first woman of Indian origin in space was:','Sunita Williams','Sirisha Bandla','Kalpana Chawla','None','c','Kalpana Chawla flew in 1997.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(849,91,'Astronauts travel to space in a:','Rocket bus','Aeroplane','Spacecraft','Helicopter','c','Astronauts use spacecraft.','easy','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(850,91,'Why does the Sun look bigger than other stars?','It is the only star','It is closer to Earth','It burns more','It moves fast','b','Distance makes Sun appear bigger.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(851,91,'Which planet is known as the Red Planet?','Earth','Venus','Mars','Jupiter','c','Mars looks reddish.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(852,91,'Planets do not have their own light because they:','Are cold','Are small','Reflect sunlight','Are far','c','Planets reflect Sun’s light.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(853,91,'Which movement causes the Moon phases?','Rotation of Sun','Revolution of Moon','Rotation of Earth','Orbit of Sun','b','Moon phases occur due to its revolution.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(854,91,'The Moon takes about how many days to revolve around Earth?','14','21','27','30','c','Moon completes in ~27 days.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(855,91,'Which planet is the third from the Sun?','Venus','Earth','Mars','Jupiter','b','Earth is third planet.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(856,91,'Why is life not possible on the Moon?','Very hot','Very cold','No air and water','Too bright','c','Life needs air and water.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(857,91,'Ursa Major is an example of:','Galaxy','Star','Planet','Constellation','d','Ursa Major is a constellation.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(858,91,'Akash Ganga is another name of:','Constellation','Planet system','Milky Way','Orbit','c','Milky Way is Akash Ganga.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(859,91,'The Sun is about how far from Earth?','1.5 lakh km','15 lakh km','1.5 crore km','15 crore km','d','Distance is about 15 crore km.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(860,91,'Which astronaut came after Kalpana Chawla?','Rakesh Sharma','Sunita Williams','Sirisha Bandla','Neil Armstrong','b','Sunita Williams flew in 2006.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(861,91,'Stars appear to twinkle because:','They move','Earth rotates','Atmosphere affects light','They are small','c','Air layers affect starlight.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(862,91,'Which object is NOT part of solar system?','Planet','Moon','Star','Tree','d','Tree is not celestial.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(863,91,'Michael Collins was a member of:','Apollo 10','Apollo 11','Apollo 12','ISS','b','He was pilot of Apollo 11.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(864,91,'Which planet is farthest from Sun?','Uranus','Saturn','Neptune','Jupiter','c','Neptune is farthest.','medium','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(865,91,'Why do we always see the same side of the Moon?','No rotation','Fast revolution','Same rotation and revolution time','Sunlight effect','c','Moon rotates and revolves in same time.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(866,91,'Which fact shows the Moon is a natural satellite?','It shines','It moves around Earth','It is big','It is bright','b','Satellites revolve around planets.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(867,91,'If today is full moon, next full moon will be after about:','15 days','21 days','29 days','31 days','c','Moon cycle is ~29 days.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(868,91,'Why are stars not visible during daytime?','They disappear','They stop shining','Sun’s bright light hides them','Earth blocks them','c','Sunlight hides starlight.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(869,91,'Which planet is called head of solar system?','Earth','Saturn','Sun','Jupiter','c','Sun controls solar system.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(870,91,'Why is the Moon’s surface full of craters?','Rain erosion','Wind erosion','Meteor impacts','Volcanoes only','c','Craters formed by impacts.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(871,91,'Why does the Moon not fall onto Earth?','Weak gravity','Same speed of rotation','Forward motion balances gravity','No force','c','Balance of motion and gravity.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(872,91,'Which statement is correct?','Sun revolves around Earth','Earth revolves around Sun','Moon revolves around Sun only','Stars revolve around Earth','b','Earth revolves around Sun.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(873,91,'Why are astronauts weightless in space?','No mass','No gravity felt','Air pressure','High speed','b','Microgravity causes weightlessness.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(874,91,'Which Indian-origin astronaut went to space in 2021?','Kalpana Chawla','Sunita Williams','Sirisha Bandla','None','c','Sirisha Bandla flew in 2021.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(875,91,'If Earth had no Moon, what would change most?','Day-night','Seasons','Tides','Gravity','c','Moon causes tides.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(876,91,'Why do constellations change position with time?','Stars move fast','Earth revolves','Sun moves','Moon phases','b','Earth’s movement changes view.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(877,91,'Which body reflects sunlight?','Star','Planet','Sun','Galaxy','b','Planets reflect sunlight.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(878,91,'Why is the Sun essential for life?','It gives light only','It gives heat and energy','It gives stars','It gives Moon','b','Life needs Sun’s energy.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39'),(879,91,'Which sequence is correct?','Star→planet→satellite','Sun→planet→moon','Moon→planet→sun','Planet→sun→moon','b','Planets revolve Sun, moons revolve planets.','hard','2026-01-17 15:34:39');
